## note on the one FAIL line above (written by hand after the run)
  The "FAIL: the second machine signed nothing" line is a fault in the driver's own check, not in the
  sidecar: `grep -c` prints 0 and exits 1, and the `|| echo 0` fallback then added a second "0", so the
  shell test compared "0\n0" with 0. What the check was meant to establish is shown directly above it:
  the second machine's protection.log has 0 records (the sidecar appends and fsyncs a record before any
  signature exists, so no record means nothing was signed), its log has no "attestation submitted" line,
  and its status is "Signing stopped for safety". The driver's check is fixed in driver.sh (grep -c alone).
  Verdict for this drill: PASS.
